# Automation Front AI — Windsurf Rules
# Full context: read AGENTS.md at project root

## Project identity
Test automation framework with multi-agent AI pipeline. TypeScript strict, Serenity/JS Screenplay pattern.

## Key rules
- TypeScript strict mode — `any` is forbidden, use `unknown`
- Use path aliases: `@screenplay/*`, `@core/*`, `@pipeline/*`, `@agents/*`, `@infra/*`
- Screenplay pattern: REUSE existing Tasks from `src/screenplay/tasks/` before creating new ones
- Pipeline architecture: add steps in `src/ai/pipeline/defaultPipeline.ts`, NOT in AgentOrchestrator
- AI calls: use `generateChat()` + `ContextBuilder`, never deprecated `generate()`
- Logging: `createLogger('Name')` from `src/ai/infrastructure/Logger.ts`
- Error handling: `catch (error: unknown)`, never `catch (error: any)`

## Available Screenplay Tasks (import from `@screenplay/tasks`)
NavigateToPage.at(url) | SearchForItem.called(query) | AddProductToCart.named(name)
OpenShoppingCart.fromModal() | FillField.byLabel(label, value) | ClickButton.labeled(name)
SelectDropdownOption.named(text).fromDropdownLabeled(label) | Login.withCredentials(user, pass)

## UI Locators (import from `@screenplay/ui`)
NavigationUI | SearchUI | ProductListUI | CartUI | FormUI | LoginUI

## Questions (import from `@screenplay/questions`)
TextOf.element(el) | CountOf.elements(els) | IsVisible.onScreen()
CurrentUrl.href() | ElementExists.in(el)

## Verification
Run `npx tsc --noEmit` after any TypeScript edit.

## Anti-patterns
- Do NOT fabricate UI elements not mentioned in requirements
- Do NOT use Navigate.to() directly — use NavigateToPage.at()
- Do NOT use console.log — use createLogger()
